Third-party dependencies retain their own licences. The full set, with licences, is
produced by:

    cd services && go tool go-licenses report ./...
    pnpm -C web licenses list

Notable choices made for licence reasons rather than technical ones:

  Valkey (BSD-3-Clause) instead of Redis. Redis 7.4 and later are RSALv2/SSPLv1, which are
  not OSI-approved. A non-OSI dependency inside an AGPL project is untenable — some
  organisations refuse them outright, and it would make this project harder to adopt for
  exactly the users it is aimed at.
